# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file: recorded risk acceptances, reviewed in PRs (PLAN.md §2.6).
# Every entry needs a reason and an expiry. `snyk ignore` rewrites this file and drops comments,
# so the full analysis lives in each `reason`.
version: v1.25.0
ignore:
  SNYK-JS-PICOMATCH-21248802:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          WHAT: picomatch ReDoS (CVE-2026-112366, CWE-1333, published 2026-10-19). A crafted
          glob pattern makes picomatch build a regex with catastrophic backtracking and pins the
          event loop. Availability only: no data read or changed.
          NO FIX: 4.0.7 and 2.3.2 are the newest releases of each line and Snyk lists no fixed
          version, so there is nothing to upgrade, patch or pnpm-override to.
          HOW IT REACHES US: typeorm > tinyglobby > picomatch@4.0.7 (and 3 similar paths).
          TypeORM only globs entity/migration paths from its options, and ours are explicit class
          lists (src/shared/database/database.ts), so no glob is ever built at runtime.
          EXPLOITABILITY: an attacker would need to control a glob pattern. No api code imports
          picomatch, micromatch or tinyglobby, and eslint.config.mjs bans those imports so a new
          use has to be argued for in review.
          REVISIT: at expiry; sooner if picomatch publishes a fix (upgrade, delete this entry) or
          if any server code starts building glob patterns from request data (then it's a real
          DoS: drop the ignore and fix it).
        expires: 2027-01-19T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z
patch: {}
